WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.790
Game of Thrones is finally on the way back
for its final season, promising to bring answers

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:09.530
to all of our questions about dragons, white
walkers, and, presumably, whether Hot Pie’s

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:11.040
new restaurant business was a success.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:15.160
Still, it’s it’s been a while since we’ve
visited the Seven Kingdoms, so before we get

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.190
the final piece of HBO’s epic hit series,
here’s a quick rundown of everything you

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:21.800
need to know before you watch Game of Thrones
Season 8.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.279
The most shattering reveal of Season 7 came
in the finale, confirming one of the longest-held

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.689
theories in all of Game of Thrones fandom.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:34.080
"General rule of thumb: Stark men don’t
fare well when they travel south."

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.920
"True, but I’m not a Stark."

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:42.370
Jon Snow is not, it turns out, the bastard
son of Ned Stark.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:48.510
He’s actually the son of Rhaegar Targaryen
and Lyanna Stark, which makes him the rightful-ish

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:49.860
heir to the Iron Throne.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.600
As his sister Lyanna was close to death due
to childbirth complications, Ned promised

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:58.880
to keep her secret at all costs, lying about
Jon’s parentage to protect his identity.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:04.100
Not even Jon knows he's a Targaryen, which
is why, in true GoT fashion, this reveal was

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:08.320
intercut with shots of Jon making out with
Daenerys Targaryen, his secret aunt.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:11.320
Surprisingly, that’s not the most shocking
thing about the scene.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:16.620
Instead, it’s the ramifications of Jon having
both Targaryen and Stark blood coursing through

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:17.360
his veins.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:22.220
As we learned from the Three-Eyed Raven, Jon’s
a walking, talking one-man song of ice and

00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:26.060
fire with roots that go back to Robert’s
Rebellion, the big brawl in Westeros that

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.800
predates the events of the series.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:33.569
Robert Baratheon cut down Rhaegar on the battlefield
and seized the Iron Throne, setting into motion

00:01:33.569 --> 00:01:37.780
the narrative we've been following for seven
seasons, but it was all based on a lie.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:42.460
When Lyanna left Robert to run off with Rhaegar,
the story throughout the Seven Kingdoms was

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:43.460
that she was kidnapped.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:49.049
In reality, though, it seems Rhaegar and Lyanna
were deeply in love, marrying in secret just

00:01:49.049 --> 00:01:50.760
before they met their ultimate fates.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:56.780
Game of Thrones has used “Winter is coming”
as its ominous tagline since 2011, and Season

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.680
7 finally delivered on that promise.

00:01:59.109 --> 00:02:03.400
As the final image of the season, we see the
undead army of White Walkers on horseback

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.940
advancing on the Seven Kingdoms.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:09.500
The woefully outmatched remnants of the free
folk and the Night's Watch helplessly watch

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:13.660
as the Night King flexes on the realms of
men by having his new ice dragon huff, puff,

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:14.840
and blow the Wall down.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:20.500
That's right: the Night King has resurrected
an undead, unkillable dragon as the deadliest

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:22.280
weapon in his considerable arsenal.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.680
So what's the deal with all the ice zombies?

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:29.300
In short, wights are the undead hordes of
soldiers who serve the White Walkers, former

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:33.040
humans turned into zombie-like ice monsters
that serve under the Night King.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:38.520
The Night King's true motives aren't yet known,
but we know that he's extremely powerful and

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.360
can control the entire army with a sort of
telepathy.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:47.300
Fire can destroy the wights, but only dragon
fire, dragonglass, and Valyrian steel can

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.440
kill White Walkers.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:53.820
Samwell Tarly has discovered that Dragonstone,
the historical seat of House Targaryen, is

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:58.370
sitting on a mountain of dragonglass, and
Jon Snow and his men have been mining it and

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:00.740
turning it into weapons in preparation ever
since.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.520
As for the Night King, it's unclear if anything
can stop him.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:09.900
In the third episode of season 7, Bran tries
to describe the Greensight for his sister

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:14.660
Sansa, telling her that it allows him to see
everything, everywhere, all at once, and also

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:18.320
that he can’t be lord of Winterfell because
he’s actually a raven.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.200
Or something like that.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.220
"It’s difficult to explain."

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:23.520
Bear with us for a moment.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:28.240
After nearly being killed back in Season 1,
Bran has visions, and those visions psychically

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:32.680
summoned him to meet the Three-Eyed Raven
north of the Wall, and while it's never been

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:37.850
officially confirmed on the show, it's implied
that the Three-Eyed Raven Bran meets is Brynden

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:40.080
Rivers, a former commander of the Night's
Watch.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:44.840
He was killed by the Night King in season
6, though, leaving Bran as the last green-seer

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.420
and the new Three-Eyed Raven.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:51.080
The scope and purpose of Bran's new powers
are yet to be revealed, but any sequence of

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:56.180
events that complicated is undoubtedly going
to play a big part in season 8's storyline.

00:03:56.860 --> 00:04:00.180
In season 7, the Stark kids have reunited
in Winterfell.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:03.100
Bran's been beyond the Wall in search of the
Three-Eyed Raven.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:07.760
Arya has been training to become the perfect
assassin with the Faceless Men before being

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.360
forced to escape their clutches.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:12.900
Sansa, however, hasn't been up to anything
nearly as cool.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:17.440
She's been used as a pawn for years, first
by the Lannisters and then in Littlefinger's

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:18.820
ongoing machinations.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:23.060
By the time she becomes the Lady of Winterfell,
finally emerging as the master manipulator

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:27.690
instead of the manipulated pawn, all three
remaining Stark children have been forever

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:28.720
transformed.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:33.520
Bran, dealing with the burden of near omnipotence,
has difficulty relating to his sisters on

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:34.300
a human level.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:37.400
Arya and Sansa are suspicious of each other's
motivations.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.800
Who can blame them for having trust issues?

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.700
Just when it seemed the Stark sisters would
succumb to paranoia and suspicion, they got

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:49.860
their act together and teamed up against their
true foe, Littlefinger himself, Lord Petyr

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:50.360
Baelish.

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:55.100
When Sansa called Arya to the Great Hall at
Littlefinger’s request, it seemed as though

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.900
she was going to accuse her sister.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:01.980
But then, when Sanas levels her charges of
murder and treason, we got the swerve.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.040
"How do you answer these charges…

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.420
Lord Baelish?"

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:14.040
Baelish believed he'd driven a wedge between
the Stark sisters, but he wasn't counting

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.690
on Bran filling in the blank parts of the
story that caused the division between Arya

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:18.300
and Sansa.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:22.660
Baelish tried to persuade her that she was
mistaken, only to be interrupted by the voice

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:27.690
of the all-seeing Three-Eyed Raven, revealing
Littlefinger's betrayal of Ned Stark way back

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:28.540
in season 1.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:33.320
That was a series wrap on Lord Baelish, as
Arya stepped up and slit the throat of what

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:37.419
was arguably the most important character
in the narrative of the series thus far.

00:05:38.419 --> 00:05:42.350
The meeting of the heaviest hitters in the
Seven Kingdoms in the ruins of the Dragonpit

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:46.490
at King’s Landing in the season 7 finale
gave the audience a taste of where everyone

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:48.540
stands in the final stretch of the great game.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:55.560
Cersei, Jaime, and Tyrion Lannister, Euron
Greyjoy, Jon Snow, Daenerys Targaryen, a dragon,

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:59.320
a White Walker, all the major players and
key elements in the struggle for the future

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:04.010
of Westeros were front and center in one of
the most intense non-battle sequences in the

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:04.500
series.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:09.520
Jon and Dany hoped to persuade the Lannisters
to at least temporarily call a truce and focus

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:12.600
on the true enemy, the Night King and his
army of White Walkers

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:26.260
Cersei, shaken by the exhibition, agrees to
the proposed truce on the condition that Jon

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:28.360
won't take up arms against the Lannisters.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:33.199
Alas, Jon Snow cannot tell a lie, he rejects
Cersei's offer, saying that he can't serve

00:06:33.199 --> 00:06:37.949
two queens, seemingly spoiling any chance
of a truce and a united force to stand against

00:06:37.949 --> 00:06:38.500
the Night King.

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:43.680
In Tyrion's last interaction with Queen Cersei,
in which he hopes to convince her to take

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:48.480
up arms against the undead army bearing down
from the North, he gets sidetracked by daring

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:49.720
Cersei to kill him.

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:53.660
"I’m about to step into a room with the
most murderous woman in the world who’s

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:56.460
already tried to kill me twice, that I know
of.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:58.320
Who’s an idiot?"

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:03.400
This is not exactly an uncommon outcome of
the Lannister siblings' conversations, but

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:08.180
this time it ends when Tyrion breaks the tense
moment by downing several glasses of wine,

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:09.040
another common outcome.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:13.520
As he attempts to find common ground with
his sister as the Hand of her rival queen,

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:17.650
Cersei reveals that her family is her only
concern, and it dawns on Tyrion that Cersei

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:18.580
is pregnant.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:23.080
Following this conversation, Cersei abruptly
declares that she'll send her armies north

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:27.540
to meet the White Walker threat, and admonishes
Tyrion to "remember my kindness."

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:30.200
Of course, that kindness comes with a nefarious
plan.

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:35.780
Cersei reveals to Jamie, her brother and the
father to her unborn child, because that’s

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:39.790
just how Westeros rolls, that she has conspired
with Euron Greyjoy.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:43.640
Instead of retreating to the Iron Islands
as he’s led everyone to believe, he's actually

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:49.510
sailing to Essos to retrieve the Golden Company:
20,000 mercenary soldiers poised to seize

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:53.360
and control Westeros while the armies of the
Seven Kingdoms kill themselves in the North.

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:57.820
Jamie, however, sees the reality of the White
Walkers’ threat, and wants nothing to do

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:59.240
with Cersei's double-cross.

00:07:59.729 --> 00:08:03.820
With Jaime leaving Cersei's side knowing the
truth of her plan, it should be interesting

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:06.280
to see what he does with this information
in season 8.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:10.980
He is driven, more than anything, by his desire
to keep the Seven Kingdoms safe for Cersei

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:11.960
and his unborn child.

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:16.580
In order to do this, he's got to take up arms
against her cause.

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:22.229
The audience last sees Jaime in season 7 riding
into the unknown as the winter's first snowfall

00:08:22.229 --> 00:08:23.300
begins in King's Landing.

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:29.240
When we last saw Melisandre, the Red Priestess
of Asshai was delivering a very cryptic farewell

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:30.680
on the cliffs of Dragonstone.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:32.180
"I've done my part.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:35.640
I've brought ice and fire together."

00:08:35.649 --> 00:08:40.250
Melisandre worships the Lord of Light, and
has shown she is capable of powerful blood

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:44.060
magic, though her powers and relationship
to the prophesied Prince That Was Promised

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:45.760
have never been fully defined.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:50.940
Her destination is likely the Red Temple of
Volantis, home to hundreds of Red Priests

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:55.880
and Priestesses, possibly with power similar
to Melisandre's own, guarded by a thousand-man

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:57.720
army known as the Fiery Hand.

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:02.080
It's theorized that Melisandre may return
to Westeros in season 8 to tip the balance

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:03.680
of power with her massive army.

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:08.940
It's worth noting that in season 6, Melisandre
was revealed to be hundreds of years old,

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:13.170
so it's quite possible that she was in Volantis
for the Doom of Valryia, the legendary collapse

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:16.240
of the advanced civilization that birthed
House Targaryen.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:20.940
In the season 7 finale, Tyrion deduces that
Cersei is pregnant.

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:25.240
The very next shot is a cut to the Dragonpit,
original site of the King's Landing Parley.

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:30.899
One fan theory suggests that, at some point
during that time lapse, Tyrion may have struck

00:09:30.899 --> 00:09:35.350
an agreement with Cersei to ensure that her
unborn child would be the king or queen to

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:36.640
succeed Daenerys.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:41.880
Tyrion believes Dany is unable to have children,
but his involvement in this plot would explain

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:46.200
his look of great concern while listening
to Jon and Dany engage in some potentially

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:48.500
baby-making behavior later in the finale.

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:55.440
Another popular theory involving Tyrion is
known as “A+J=T,” or Aerys plus Joanna

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:56.440
equals Tyrion.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:10:01.860
George R.R. Martin's books often mention the
Mad King Aerys' lust for Tywin Lannister's

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:05.260
wife, Joanna, and Joanna died while giving
birth to Tyrion.

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:10.480
If it's true that Aerys is Tyrion's true father,
it could provide another reason for Tywin’s

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:14.540
lifelong hatred for Tyrion and give a whole
new meaning to Tywin's final words to him

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:16.580
"You're no son of mine!"

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:21.440
Tyrion’s been a fan favorite since the very
first episode, so perhaps we'll see him riding

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:24.300
a dragon off into the sunset to close out
this epic tale.

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:26.880
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:29.800
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:33.040
Subscribe to our YouTube channel, and hit
the bell so you don't miss a single one.

